        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ffbe6d29-0012-5e27-a960-4da878d81fee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Liddell, Harold Abrahams, Evelyn Aubrey Montague\n- Organizations: Achilles Club\n- Products: Chariots of Fire\n- Events: 1924 Olympics\n- Concepts: Christianity, Judaism, prejudice, missionary work\n\nFacts:\n- Eric Henry Liddell was born on 16 January 1902 and later became a Scottish athlete, a rugby union international player, and a missionary.\n- The 1924 Olympics are depicted in the film \"Chariots of Fire\" through the fact-based story of two athletes, Eric Liddell and Harold Abrahams.\n- In \"Chariots of Fire,\" Eric Liddell is portrayed as a devout Scottish Christian who runs for the glory of God.\n- In \"Chariots of Fire,\" Harold Abrahams is portrayed as an English Jew who runs to overcome prejudice.\n- Eric Liddell chose his religious beliefs over competing in an Olympic race that was held on a Sunday.\n- Evelyn Aubrey Montague was one of the founding members of the Achilles Club.\n- Evelyn Aubrey Montague was immortalized in the 1981 film \"Chariots of Fire.\"\n- Eric Henry Liddell died on 21 February 1945.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
